From 7bf12d8c94cf252b807e83628f022ea1febeefa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:43:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed configured database and UTXO cache
 budgets

Convert all five shared startup cache-budget LogInfo producers while
retaining their original arithmetic, Info/ALL level/category and exact
.1f MiB text. Database budgets have a distinct FLOAT field and stable
purposeful event names; filter Name preserves BlockFilterTypeName. The
UTXO memory budget uses the existing UTXOCacheMiB key, alongside a new
FLOAT field for the original unused-mempool budget. These are configured
budgets in MiB, not observed resident use or byte counts.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py 0.51.0, from the parent checkout):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/node-cache-budgets.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/node-cache-budgets-applied.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/init.cpp

Explicit support: append two FLOAT registry keys without changing old
IDs. Retain the registry macro's existing one-entry-per-line convention.
Add a focused wallet-less functional fixture that enables both indexes
and sets a nondefault cache budget, then verifies all five actual JSON
producers, numeric units, names, Info levels and readable precision after
shutdown flushes the logger. The fixture is reviewed test code rather
than a claimed generated conversion.

Source checks: converter15 fixtures and idempotence, production event
lint307, Ruff0.15.8 and whitespace pass. Native build/runtime are pending
separate receipts; no behavioral or benchmark pass is claimed here.
Shared eCash owner; V2 inherits unchanged.
